  Keep the two in step: any file added here must also be added to the matching
  source list in CMakeLists.txt, and vice versa.

  WHY THIS FILE LIVES IN vs/ RATHER THAN BESIDE src/:
  Visual Studio offers every file under a project's directory as something to
  add to that project, and it repeatedly swept tests\*.cpp into pm.exe. Each
  time, the link broke with "main ist bereits in main.obj definiert", because
  tests\test_main.cpp carries the test runner's own main(). With the project
  files in their own directory there is nothing beside them to sweep.

  Settings deliberately matched to the CMake build:
    - x64 only (spec S3); the Win32 configurations are intentionally absent
    - C++20, /permissive-, /W4, /utf-8
    - static CRT, so pm.exe needs no redistributable (spec S2)
    - ..\src on the include path, which is what the "core/..." includes resolve
      against

  MSBuild puts every object file of a project in one flat intermediate
  directory, so no two .cpp files here may share a basename. Generated by
  scratchpad/gen_vs.py.
-->
